You're really fighting it now, the high wire starts acting like a jump rope. Oops, the gorilla suit goes flying.
You're doing a pretty good Elvis right before you plummet ...

... to an inglorious circus death.

    ****  You have died  ****

Well not quite died. The doctors do what they can, but as the debts rise and the prognosis dips you take the only avenue left -- and sell yourself to the circus.

As "The Human Platypus," you enjoy top billing as a popular midway attraction, garnering fame to rival that of nineteenth century oddity John Merrick.

Still, as the fingers of the Great Unwashed poke at your benumbed hide, you contemplate how this fate might have been thwarted.

